  "repository_path": "src/boundary_clip_legacy",
  "runtime_dependencies": "Existing clipper2-rust integer-point types and the Rust standard library.",
  "local_implementation_changes": [
    "Local minima retain arena insertion IDs; their linked list is ordered once at reset by descending integer Y and descending insertion ID, preserving classic newest-first equal-Y ties.",
    "Initial reset scanbeams are appended and deduplicated from that ordered list, preserving scanbeam IDs, Y values, links and edge-reset order; sweep-time scanbeam insertion is unchanged.",
    "The temporary minima-index allocation is fallible and reports a private clipping error on refusal.",
    "Tile/TIN clipping retains legacy crossing sorting; the flat global merge explicitly selects modern introsort, matching the respective managed host policies without a runtime dependency.",
    "Four join predicates use original edge-delta collinearity from the licensed 6.2.1 source rather than rounded current-point slopes."
  ],
